WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.033
-Our first guest
is a country-music superstar

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:05.234
whose new album
"Body Language (Deluxe),"

00:00:05.234 --> 00:00:06.667
is out tomorrow.

00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:08.601
He's also a great coach
on "The Voice,"

00:00:08.601 --> 00:00:12.100
which airs Mondays and Tuesdays
at 8:00 p.m., on NBC.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:15.801
Please welcome,
the one and only, Blake Shelton.

00:00:15.801 --> 00:00:17.300
♪♪

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.601
[ Cheers and applause ]
Wow.

00:00:19.601 --> 00:00:21.968
Blake.

00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:23.167
Thank you for being here,

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:25.634
and thank you
for playing a game.

00:00:25.634 --> 00:00:28.901
Because I just -- we saw each
other recently, in person.

00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:31.367
-Yeah.
-You helped me out on my show,

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:34.334
"That's My Jam,"
and we played some games.

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:36.667
And I just know --
You had fun, right?

00:00:36.667 --> 00:00:39.200
-Oh, yeah,
and now you're helping me out

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.834
by having me
play more of your games...

00:00:41.834 --> 00:00:43.200
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.300
...on the show.
Thanks for the opportunities.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.000
[ Laughter ]
I appreciate it.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.501
-I will say, you were
a good sport on the show,

00:00:50.501 --> 00:00:52.334
and I appreciate you doing it.

00:00:52.334 --> 00:00:54.200
Although, I think
you do have to brush up

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.467
on your Taylor Swift songs.

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:58.367
-Yeah.
-Yeah, because you --

00:00:58.367 --> 00:00:59.701
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.701 --> 00:01:00.934
You didn't really know that.

00:01:00.934 --> 00:01:03.367
But I'm assuming
you must have run into

00:01:03.367 --> 00:01:04.934
each other in Nashville,
or something.

00:01:04.934 --> 00:01:08.033
-Look, listen to me,
there's Taylor Swift --

00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:10.400
there's the country
Taylor Swift,

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.868
which I know some of that.
-Yeah.

00:01:12.868 --> 00:01:18.033
-I'm not as familiar
with the new Taylor Swift 2.0,

00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:20.868
which is, you know,
the pop version, you know?

00:01:20.868 --> 00:01:22.934
I'm still --
I'm still stuck when she was

00:01:22.934 --> 00:01:24.133
doing her country records.
-Yeah.

00:01:24.133 --> 00:01:27.033
You think you --
-You don't do any country music

00:01:27.033 --> 00:01:29.367
on "That's My Jam," by the way.

00:01:29.367 --> 00:01:33.901
Because you had Ariana there,
and so you were totally

00:01:33.901 --> 00:01:37.567
sucking up to Ariana
and trying throw music at her

00:01:37.567 --> 00:01:39.367
that you thought
she would guess.

00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:40.767
-That's not true.
-And little did you know

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:43.367
that Kelly Clarkson
is such a nerd

00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:45.601
that she knows every song
on the planet,

00:01:45.601 --> 00:01:49.567
because she sings a different
song on her show every day.

00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:52.000
So she knows every word
to every song.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.000
-Yeah, but, also, I know,
by talking to you,

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.334
you're like
a musical encyclopedia.

00:01:56.334 --> 00:01:59.400
I could name a song, and you
could tell me who sings it.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:03.734
Like, who sings
"The Piña Colada Song"?

00:02:03.734 --> 00:02:04.968
-Rupert Holmes.

00:02:04.968 --> 00:02:06.901
-How the heck
could you know that?

00:02:06.901 --> 00:02:09.100
-Well, I just happened
to know that one.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:11.434
That was a lucky guess.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.434 --> 00:02:13.434
-No, you're fantastic.
So I figured --

00:02:13.434 --> 00:02:16.267
So when we were playing
the game, I had you sing

00:02:16.267 --> 00:02:18.434
the theme from
"The Golden Girls."

00:02:18.434 --> 00:02:20.067
I thought that was --
-I did.

00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:22.534
I felt like I did a good job
on that, by the way.

00:02:22.534 --> 00:02:24.133
-You crushed it.
-I mean, I don't want to --

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:26.033
I don't want to brag, but...
-Too late.

00:02:26.033 --> 00:02:27.367
Too late --
you already bragged.

00:02:27.367 --> 00:02:28.534
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:02:28.534 --> 00:02:30.801
I want to talk to you about
the new album.

00:02:30.801 --> 00:02:33.400
I want to talk about
"Body Language (Deluxe)."

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:35.667
But first, I want to talk about
your wedding.

00:02:35.667 --> 00:02:36.801
Look at this.

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:39.033
Look at the beautiful couple
right here.

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:40.534
Look at that.
-Oh.

00:02:40.534 --> 00:02:41.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:41.534 --> 00:02:44.334
Unbelievable.
-You know...

00:02:44.334 --> 00:02:47.701
-Beautiful.
-Gwen and I agreed that

00:02:47.701 --> 00:02:51.067
we like to take our
publicity stunts all the way.

00:02:51.067 --> 00:02:53.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.033 --> 00:02:55.734
So we thought we would go ahead
and just seal the deal.

00:02:55.734 --> 00:02:57.234
-That's so funny.
-Know what I'm saying?

00:02:57.234 --> 00:02:59.234
-It looked great.
I just thought it was

00:02:59.234 --> 00:03:01.100
a beautiful -- everything
I've seen and things --

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:03.133
I mean, I didn't hear from you
or anything,

00:03:03.133 --> 00:03:06.033
you know, personally, and say,
"Hey, Jimmy, what are you doing?

00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:07.934
Are you busy this week?"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.934 --> 00:03:10.501
You know what?
Not much planning went into it.

00:03:10.501 --> 00:03:11.801
I understand.

00:03:11.801 --> 00:03:13.300
Who puts planning
into a wedding, you know?

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:14.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.834 --> 00:03:18.868
Anyway, I just remember
not being invited, and I go --

00:03:18.868 --> 00:03:23.901
-We only had room
for one NBC host at the wedding,

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:26.701
so we had Carson.
-Yeah, Carson Daly was there.

00:03:26.701 --> 00:03:29.033
That's true, yeah.
But I've known you and Gwen

00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:30.767
for a long time,
and I just figured, you know...

00:03:30.767 --> 00:03:32.667
I didn't figure anything,
really, you know?

00:03:32.667 --> 00:03:35.367
I was just sitting at home,
trying to, like, see --

00:03:35.367 --> 00:03:37.434
read on Twitter
how's the wedding going.

00:03:37.434 --> 00:03:40.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:44.834
Anyway, it seemed like a blast.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.834 --> 00:03:48.667
Uh...
[ Laughter continues ]

00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:50.434
Did you save me a piece of cake
or anything?

00:03:50.434 --> 00:03:51.767
I mean, maybe that, you sent --

00:03:51.767 --> 00:03:53.200
Please don't
send me that banana.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:55.434
-You're always trying to make me
feel like Super Dave Osborne.

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:56.601
Remember Super Dave Osborne?
-No, I do not.

00:03:56.601 --> 00:03:58.634
I do not, I do not.
-You do that every time.

00:03:58.634 --> 00:04:00.200
We talked about this last time.
-No, I don't.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.467
-And I end up coming across
as the grumpy guy.

00:04:02.467 --> 00:04:05.667
Trying to be festive,
wearing a Santa hat,

00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:07.701
and then you just kick me
in the nuts over and over

00:04:07.701 --> 00:04:08.901
on national television.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:08.901 --> 00:04:10.934
-How can you be mad at --

00:04:10.934 --> 00:04:13.167
How could you be mad
at this little guy?

00:04:13.167 --> 00:04:15.267
Look at this little guy.

00:04:15.267 --> 00:04:16.567
Aww.
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:04:16.567 --> 00:04:18.000
Look, that's you and Gwen.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.100
-That's back when Gwen and I
used to be brother and sister.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:24.801
[ Laughter, audience groans ]

00:04:24.801 --> 00:04:26.334
Way back in the day.

00:04:26.334 --> 00:04:27.434
[ Laughter continues ]

00:04:27.434 --> 00:04:32.667
-Oh, my God!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:33.834
-You know, that was years ago.

00:04:33.834 --> 00:04:36.767
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.767 --> 00:04:39.901
-Dude, you're unbelievable.
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:39.901 --> 00:04:43.133
But when you --

00:04:43.133 --> 00:04:45.367
When you did your own vows
for the wedding...

00:04:45.367 --> 00:04:46.634
-Yeah.
-...you surprised Gwen,

00:04:46.634 --> 00:04:48.767
and you actually sang your vows.

00:04:48.767 --> 00:04:50.467
Is that correct?
-I did.

00:04:50.467 --> 00:04:53.968
Well, Carson told me that --
He told both of us

00:04:53.968 --> 00:04:58.501
that he expected us to write our
vows for the wedding and --

00:04:58.501 --> 00:05:02.667
which is a lot of pressure.
Because, you know,

00:05:02.667 --> 00:05:08.334
as easy as it is for Gwen and I
to get up and sing, you know,

00:05:08.334 --> 00:05:12.567
to, like, write something down
and say it is really awkward.

00:05:12.567 --> 00:05:15.234
And so I just copped out,
went ahead,

00:05:15.234 --> 00:05:17.601
and wrote something down
that I could sing.

00:05:17.601 --> 00:05:20.033
And so I wrote this song.
I wrote it with a buddy

00:05:20.033 --> 00:05:21.567
named Craig Wiseman, actually,

00:05:21.567 --> 00:05:25.200
and it's on this album
that comes out.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:27.167
It comes out tomorrow, I think.
-That's correct.

00:05:27.167 --> 00:05:28.934
-When does this air?
Does this air tonight?

00:05:28.934 --> 00:05:29.968
Are we live?

00:05:29.968 --> 00:05:31.467
-You don't know
when my show airs?

00:05:31.467 --> 00:05:33.667
Yeah, it's on eve--
"The Tonight Show."

00:05:33.667 --> 00:05:35.501
At this point,
your album is out.

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:38.501
It's past midnight.
-You come on after --

00:05:38.501 --> 00:05:41.534
Who do you come on after?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.534 --> 00:05:44.734
Anyway, I don't know
if it's midnight or --

00:05:44.734 --> 00:05:46.467
-It is now midnight.
It's now midnight.

00:05:46.467 --> 00:05:48.367
It's past midnight,
and this album is out.

00:05:48.367 --> 00:05:50.968
"Body Language (Deluxe)"
is out right now.

00:05:50.968 --> 00:05:52.434
This is out.
It's available.

00:05:52.434 --> 00:05:55.501
[ Cheers and applause ]
You can get the song.

00:05:55.501 --> 00:05:59.367
"We Can Reach the Stars."
-That's the song.

00:05:59.367 --> 00:06:01.767
That's the song
I wrote for Gwen Stefani.

00:06:01.767 --> 00:06:03.234
-Wow.
-My wife.

00:06:03.234 --> 00:06:06.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I love that.

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:09.267
-I hear the mixed reaction there
in the studio audience.

00:06:09.267 --> 00:06:10.968
[ Laughter ]
Like, there was a few gasps.

00:06:10.968 --> 00:06:12.834
-A little bummed out
because we thought --

00:06:12.834 --> 00:06:14.100
Which one did you write for me?

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:17.567
Was it
"Monday Morning Missing You"?

00:06:17.567 --> 00:06:19.667
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.667 --> 00:06:20.868
Or was it "Corn"?
-No.

00:06:20.868 --> 00:06:24.434
-Was it "Corn"?
-No, but --

00:06:24.434 --> 00:06:25.934
-Don't you --
Please don't bring out the --

00:06:25.934 --> 00:06:27.400
Oh, my God. Please don't
bring out that banana.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:30.834
-I'm really inspired by this.
-Get rid of that stupid thing!

00:06:30.834 --> 00:06:33.133
Get rid of that dumb thing.
-I'm really inspired by this.

00:06:33.133 --> 00:06:35.767
I think we should
write a song about it.

00:06:35.767 --> 00:06:37.534
-I want to talk to you about
"The Voice" when we come back.

00:06:37.534 --> 00:06:38.634
All right,
more with Blake Shelton,

00:06:38.634 --> 00:06:39.968
everybody, when we come back.

